# screen time

Monitors X Window screen state and logs switches.

## Installation

This depends on `xset` application and is useless if DPMS is not enabled.

Just copy the script and add something like this into your `.xinitrc`:

  # turn off the screen after 2 minutes of inactivity
  xset dpms 0 120 0
  python $HOME/scripts/screen_time.py &

## Logging

It logs into `$HOME/screentime.jsonl` and entries look like this:

  {"boot_at": "2026-09-07 09:17:55", "started_at": "2026-09-07 09:20:10", "ended_at": "2026-09-07 14:20:50", "total_on": "0:45:00", "total_off": "4:15:30", "switches": ["2026-09-07 09:20:10", "2026-09-07 09:30:41", "2026-09-07 13:29:09", "2026-09-07 13:33:49"]}

